[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2874131223","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106316#issuecomment-2874131223","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106316","id":2874131223,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rT8MX","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-12T21:16:54Z","updated_at":"2025-05-12T22:31:33Z","body":"See also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/79733. If this PR is merged, I'll probably make it so my PR treats light values as transparent (and dark values as opaque) for masking. This means pixels that are closer to the camera will appear more tinted in red.\r\n\r\nWe should also see if we can make the debug view use nearest-neighbor filtering instead of bilinear filtering, as occlusion culling is an \"all or nothing\" thing.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2874131223/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2875398446","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106316#issuecomment-2875398446","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106316","id":2875398446,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rYxku","user":{"login":"Rudolph-B","id":52322745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzIyNzQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52322745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B","html_url":"https://github.com/Rudolph-B","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T07:42:33Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T07:42:33Z","body":">We should also see if we can make the debug view use nearest-neighbor filtering instead of bilinear filtering, as occlusion culling is an \"all or nothing\" thing.\r\n\r\nI think nearest-neighbor works well when camera jitter is disabled, but with it enabled the effect is a bit jarring for me.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b3ae85f1-e4a1-4ad9-8d2a-32f5adeed4c5\r\n\r\nWhat do you think?\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2875398446/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2875441538","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106316#issuecomment-2875441538","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106316","id":2875441538,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rY8GC","user":{"login":"snowflower","id":1240280,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNDAyODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1240280?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower","html_url":"https://github.com/snowflower","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T07:58:39Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T07:58:39Z","body":"is it possible to expose the debug texture source with this depth information (Through the Rendering Server ?) so someone could assign the texture to a sprite2D and debug draw with it using their own visualization shader?\r\n\r\nThis would allow some customization for how the user wants to display it, such as controlling the blending mode+alpha, customizing a gradient map, or offsetting and scaling it down to the corner of the screen like a picture-in-picture mode.\r\n\r\nOther useful examples are to multiply the depth and then apply fract() before outputting the color giving a zebra-stripe depth banding thats high contrast and works for a large depth range\r\n*or* reconstructing the world position from depth and using fract on worldpos xyz to create a colored 3d 'grid' - these are useful accessibility visualizations that can be easier to overlay occlusion buffer information on more complex textured and lit scenes.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2875441538/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2875557000","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106316#issuecomment-2875557000","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106316","id":2875557000,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rZYSI","user":{"login":"snowflower","id":1240280,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNDAyODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1240280?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower","html_url":"https://github.com/snowflower","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T08:36:59Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T08:36:59Z","body":"> > We should also see if we can make the debug view use nearest-neighbor filtering instead of bilinear filtering, as occlusion culling is an \"all or nothing\" thing.\r\n> \r\n> I think nearest-neighbor works well when camera jitter is disabled, but with it enabled the effect is a bit jarring for me.\r\n> \r\n>  Jitter-Nearest.mp4 \r\n> What do you think?\r\n\r\nIs there a reason why the Jitter Projection has to require saving my work, and restarting the editor?\r\nToggling the occlusion culling system on/off does not require a restart so I find it strange that the jittering does.\r\n\r\nI find myself just running the editor with the jitter turned OFF because its pretty fatiguing to look at it for extended periods of time making levels and looking at the occlusion buffer results.\r\nA runtime toggle for the jitter that doesnt require a restart would be useful to compare a camera view of a world scene in a game to see if the jitter on/off creates significant different occlusion behavior and performance differences.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2875557000/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2876987535","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106316#issuecomment-2876987535","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106316","id":2876987535,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6re1iP","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T15:30:57Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T15:30:57Z","body":"> I think nearest-neighbor works well when camera jitter is disabled, but with it enabled the effect is a bit jarring for me.\r\n\r\nMaybe occlusion culling jitter should be disabled while in the debug view.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2876987535/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2877044321","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106316#issuecomment-2877044321","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106316","id":2877044321,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rfDZh","user":{"login":"Rudolph-B","id":52322745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzIyNzQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52322745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B","html_url":"https://github.com/Rudolph-B","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T15:49:27Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T15:50:09Z","body":"> is it possible to expose the debug texture source with this depth information (Through the Rendering Server ?) so someone could assign the texture to a sprite2D and debug draw with it using their own visualization shader?\r\n\r\nI doubt it is exposed at the moment and discussing exposing it should rather happen in a proposal since it is a significant change.\r\n\r\n>Is there a reason why the Jitter Projection has to require saving my work, and restarting the editor?\r\nToggling the occlusion culling system on/off does not require a restart so I find it strange that the jittering does.\r\n\r\nAs far as I can see there exist no explicit reason (The entire occlusion pipeline gets freed and rebuilt when you toggle occlusion culling in project settings). It definitely would improve workflow to not to require the restart. Changing it just isn't trivial and might take some work.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2877044321/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2877122739","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106316#issuecomment-2877122739","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106316","id":2877122739,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rfWiz","user":{"login":"Rudolph-B","id":52322745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzIyNzQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52322745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://ap